{
  "name": "what every model file must be",
  "why": "The format ai_learning's ModelFile reads and gameaikit.training.model_file writes, held to one answer per file in both languages: the code of the first rule it breaks, or the models it publishes and the fields beside them.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "why": "The smallest file there is: one model and nothing else. No game's fields, and nothing asks for any.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "chance": {
            "kind": "logistic",
            "features": [
              "my_health",
              "their_health"
            ],
            "weights": [
              0.05,
              -0.05
            ],
            "bias": 0.5
          }
        }
      },
      "loads": [
        "chance"
      ],
      "extra": []
    },
    {
      "why": "Fields beside `models` are the publishing game's. They are handed over unread, and a file is not refused for carrying them.",
      "file": {
        "generated_by": "somebody's trainer",
        "my_radius": 3,
        "models": {
          "b": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          },
          "a": {
            "kind": "logistic",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "loads": [
        "a",
        "b"
      ],
      "extra": [
        "generated_by",
        "my_radius"
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "Not JSON at all.",
      "text": "weights: lots\n",
      "refused": "M2"
    },
    {
      "why": "JSON, but a list: there is nowhere for `models` to be.",
      "text": "[1, 2]\n",
      "refused": "M2"
    },
    {
      "why": "An object with no models.",
      "file": {},
      "refused": "M3"
    },
    {
      "why": "A `models` that publishes none.",
      "file": {
        "models": {}
      },
      "refused": "M3"
    },
    {
      "why": "A `models` that is a list rather than names to models.",
      "file": {
        "models": [
          {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        ]
      },
      "refused": "M3"
    },
    {
      "why": "A model that is not an object at all. Found missing by review: this rule could once be deleted with every gate green.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "combat": "0.5, probably"
        }
      },
      "refused": "M10"
    },
    {
      "why": "A model with no bias. Defaulting it to 0 is a model nobody fitted.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M4"
    },
    {
      "why": "A model with no kind.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M4"
    },
    {
      "why": "A kind nothing here can evaluate, named rather than guessed at: quietly treating it as linear would answer with great confidence.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "random_forest",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M5"
    },
    {
      "why": "A model looking at nothing.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [],
            "weights": [],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M6"
    },
    {
      "why": "A feature name that is a number. Rows are matched by name, and this one matches nothing a game can build.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              7
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M6"
    },
    {
      "why": "A feature listed twice: a weight that can never be applied.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one",
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0,
              2.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M6"
    },
    {
      "why": "One weight short.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one",
              "two"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M7"
    },
    {
      "why": "Weights that are not a list.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": 1.0,
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M7"
    },
    {
      "why": "A weight that is a word.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              "heavy"
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M8"
    },
    {
      "why": "A bias that is `true`: a yes, not a number, in both languages.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": true
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M8"
    },
    {
      "why": "A bias JSON cannot spell but can still carry: 1e400 parses to infinity, which multiplies every feature into one answer.",
      "text": "{\"models\": {\"only\": {\"kind\": \"linear\", \"features\": [\"one\"], \"weights\": [1.0], \"bias\": 1e400}}}\n",
      "refused": "M8"
    },
    {
      "why": "`NaN` is not JSON, though Python's reader accepts it unless told not to: both languages refuse the text, not the number.",
      "text": "{\"models\": {\"only\": {\"kind\": \"linear\", \"features\": [\"one\"], \"weights\": [NaN], \"bias\": 0.0}}}\n",
      "refused": "M2"
    },
    {
      "why": "Nor is `Infinity`, for the same reason.",
      "text": "{\"models\": {\"only\": {\"kind\": \"linear\", \"features\": [\"one\"], \"weights\": [1.0], \"bias\": -Infinity}}}\n",
      "refused": "M2"
    },
    {
      "why": "An integer too big for a float, with no exponent: the game reads infinity, and Python must not crash converting it.",
      "text": "{\"models\": {\"only\": {\"kind\": \"linear\", \"features\": [\"one\"], \"weights\": [], \"bias\": 0.0}}}\n",
      "refused": "M8"
    },
    {
      "why": "A sound first model does not excuse a broken second: the file is refused whole.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "first": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          },
          "second": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one",
              "two"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M7"
    },
    {
      "why": "A weight that is `false`: a yes-or-no inside the numbers.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              false
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M8"
    },
    {
      "why": "A kind that is a number, not a name.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": 7,
            "features": [
              "one"
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M5"
    },
    {
      "why": "A name listed twice before a name that is not a string: the first wrong name is the one reported, in both languages.",
      "file": {
        "models": {
          "only": {
            "kind": "linear",
            "features": [
              "a",
              "a",
              1
            ],
            "weights": [
              1.0,
              1.0,
              1.0
            ],
            "bias": 0.0
          }
        }
      },
      "refused": "M6"
    }
  ]
}
